      "source": "https://www.visitmaconcountymo.com/excello"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the 1880s Excello had become a bustling railroad station and coal‑mining camp, shipping ore to larger markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitmaconcountymo.com/excello"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits eight miles south of Macon, sixteen miles north of Moberly, just west of U.S. Route 50.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excello%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Excello rests on high ground that drains west toward the East Fork of the Little Chariton River and east toward Hoover Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
